# The ASCII face of the stale-match bug (round-7 hunt): with no
# multi-byte text to trip over, Shift+F3 selected the old bytes 0..3 —
# three of the four indent spaces — and typing replaced them, leaving
# "Z abchello". The match is found again at its new offset first.
write f.txt "hello\n"
open f.txt
type abc
key ctrl+f
type abc
key ctrl+]
key shift+f3
key esc
type Z
key ctrl+s
expect file f.txt contains "    Zhello"
